; NextDAAD debugger kit fixture, part 1. Built by the kit (lib\debug.ps1) for
; autopilot leg K. GO A and GO B are written apart over identical bodies, so
; the compiler shares the bytes and each line keeps its own owner; SEE A and
; SEE B are synonym headers over one body. One condact per line.
/CTL
_
/VOC
GO    30  verb
SEE   31  verb
PUSH  32  verb
HIT   33  verb
SWITCH 34 verb
A     10  noun
B     11  noun
/STX
/0  "It's too dark to see anything."
/1  "I can also see:"
/2  "What now?"
/3  "What next?"
/4  "What should I do now?"
/5  "What should I do next?"
/6  "I didn't understand."
/7  "I can't go in that direction."
/8  "I can't do that."
/9  "I have with me:"
/10 "I am wearing:"
/11 " "
/12 "Are you sure?"
/13 "Another go?"
/14 " "
/15 "OK."
/16 "Press any key."
/17 " "
/18 " "
/19 " "
/20 " "
/21 " "
/22 " "
/23 "I'm not wearing one of those."
/24 "I can't. My hands are full."
/25 "I already have the _."
/26 "There isn't one of those here."
/27 "I can't carry any more things."
/28 "I don't have one of those."
/29 "I'm already wearing the _."
/30 "Y"
/31 "N"
/32 "More..."
/33 ">"
/34 " "
/35 " "
/36 "I now have the _."
/37 "I'm now wearing the _."
/38 "I've removed the _."
/39 "I've dropped the _."
/40 "I can't wear the _."
/41 "I can't remove the _."
/42 "I can't remove the _. My hands are full."
/43 "The _ weighs too much for me."
/44 "The _ is in the"
/45 "The _ isn't in the"
/46 ", "
/47 " and "
/48 ".#n"
/49 "I don't have the _."
/50 "I'm not wearing the _."
/51 "."
/52 "There isn't one of those in the"
/53 "Nothing."
/54 " "
/55 " "
/56 " "
/57 "I/O Error"
/58 " "
/59 "File name error."
/60 "Type in name of file."
/MTX
/0  "DBGKIT part one."
/1  "INDIR line ran."
/2  "Shared condact ran."
/3  " "
/4  " "
/5  " "
/6  " "
/7  " "
/8  " "
/9  " "
/10 "Entry A ran."
/11 "Entry B ran."
/12 "Synonym body ran."
/OTX
/0 "a stone"
/LTX
/0 "Hall."
/CON
/0
/OBJ
/0  252   1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   _ _
/PRO 0
> _ _   ZERO 102
        SET 102
        MESSAGE 0
> _ _   PARSE 0
        SYSMESS 6
        REDO
> _ _   CLS
        PROCESS 1
        REDO
/PRO 1
> GO A  MESSAGE @34
        DONE
> GO B  MESSAGE @34
        DONE
> SEE A
> SEE B MESSAGE @34
        MESSAGE 12
        DONE
> PUSH _  LET 101 1
          LET 100 @101
          MESSAGE @100
          DONE
#include inc/SHARED.DSF
> SWITCH _  EXTERN 2 4
            DONE
> _ _   SYSMESS 8
        DONE
/END
